==English==

===Etymology===
{{etyl|fro|en}} {{term|aquest|lang=fro}}, (French {{term|acquêt|lang=fr}}), from {{etyl|LL.|en}} {{term|acquestum|lang=la}}, {{term|acquisitum|acquisītum|lang=la}}, for Latin {{term|acquisitum|acquisītum|lang=la}}, past participle (used substantively) of {{term|acquirere||lang=la|to acquire}}. See {{l/en|acquire}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{context|rare}} [[acquisition|Acquisition]]; the thing gained.
#: {{rfquotek|Francis Bacon}}
# {{context|legal}} property acquired by purchase, gift, or otherwise than by inheritance.
#: {{rfquotek|John Bouvier}}

====Usage notes====
Bouvier, 1856, [http://www.constitution.org/bouv/bouvier_a.htm] from which the Webster derives, uses the spelling ''[[acquets]]''.

